# Installation docs — no duplication

When editing pages under `docs/installation/` (especially `orchestrator-requirements/`):

- **Do not repeat** content already covered on shared pages.
- **Link** to the canonical page (prefer `target="_blank"` + `rel="noopener noreferrer"` for cross-page links from orchestrator-requirements checklists).

## Canonical pages

| Topic | Link to |
|---|---|
| Hosting / VM topology | `/installation/hosting-topology` |
| VM specs, ports, partitions, inter-VM ports | `/installation/prerequisites` |
| Domain / DNS / URLs | `/installation/prerequisites#domain-name--url` (FAQ on same page) |
| CloudStack Console Proxy DNS | `/installation/orchestrator-requirements/cloudstack#7-console-proxy-domain-dns` |
| SSL / TLS certificates | `/installation/prerequisites#ssl--tls-certificates` |
| SMTP | `/installation/prerequisites#smtp--email-configuration` |
| App logos | `/installation/prerequisites#app-logos` |
| StackConsole team access (common) | `/installation/prerequisites#access-for-stackconsole-installation-team` |
| Payment gateways | `/billing/payment-gateways/` |

Orchestrator-requirements pages should keep **orchestrator-specific** content only (e.g. CloudStack DomainAdmin credentials, Featured/Public templates, CloudStack checkpoints). For shared install inputs, use a short “see …” section with links — not full tables or field lists. Do **not** paste Currency / Payment Gateway / Other Settings billing blocks from requirement templates — link to billing docs instead.
